      "content": "For incorporating neighborhood stability and community cohesion, I suggest a phased approach starting with feature engineering to quantify these concepts from publicly available data. Weighting should be determined through rigorous backtesting, where you test various combinations of weights against historical default data. Begin by assigning moderate initial weights and then use techniques like Lasso or regularization to see which features have the most predictive power in your model.",
